molecule metabolic substrate and network architecture, continuing with cofactors and key conserved reactions, and culminating in the aggregation of multiple diverse physical and biochemical processes in cells."}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/W7154867203", "doi": null, "title": "Signature of the Trinity How Science’s Deepest Patterns Reveal God’s Design", "publication_year": null, "type": "book", "cited_by_count": 0, "open_access": {"is_oa": true, "oa_status": "green", "oa_url": "https://philpapers.org/archive/BARSOT-29.pdf", "any_repository_has_fulltext": true}, "primary_location": {"id": "pmh:oai:philarchive.org/rec/BARSOT-29", "doi": null, "is_oa": true, "landing_page_url": "https://philarchive.org/rec/BARSOT-29", "pdf_url": "https://philpapers.org/archive/BARSOT-29.pdf", "source": {"id": "https://openalex.org/S4306402130", "display_name": "PhilPapers (PhilPapers Foundation)", "issn_l": null, "issn": null, "is_oa": false, "is_in_doaj": false, "is_core": false, "listed_in": [], "host_organization": null, "host_organization_name": null, "host_organization_lineage": [], "host_organization_lineage_names": [], "type": "repository"}, "license": null, "license_id": null, "version": "submittedVersion", "is_accepted": false, "is_published": false, "raw_source_name": null, "raw_type": "info:eu-repo/semantics/book"}, "abstract": "What if a nineteenth century theologian foresaw the findings of modern science? What if the most stubborn puzzles in science, wave and particle, relativity and quantum mechanics, entropy and order, aren’t failures to be solved, but signatures to be read? Signature of the Trinity tells this story. For over a century, physicists have chased a “theory of everything” yet the deepest structures of reality refuse to collapse into a single principle. Instead, they persist as irreducible, complementary opposites that are jointly indispensable. This book argues that this is no accident. From quantum physics to cosmology, from genetics to consciousness, the same relational architecture appears: unity with internal distinction. Signature of the Trinity makes a bold, testable claim: the pervasive pattern of explanatory twofoldness across science is best explained by an ultimate reality that is itself a differentiated unity, the Triune God. If you’re ready to see science and theology converge in a way that is intellectually rigorous, historically rooted, and spiritually compelling, this book will change how you see the World and the God who made it."}]", "excerpt_truncated": true, "source_sha256": "97ad01a287e12cbe5170b23190fe5b2b563c84b053747c9da9f0ebd4d15bb75a", "verification_required": true, "topic_domain": "chemical_heredity", "evidence_role": "discovery", "host_tier": "discovery", "source_identity": null, "persistent_identifiers": ["doi:10.3390/life11040308", "openalex:W3144837547", "openalex:W7154867203"], "source_candidates": ["https://doi.org/10.3390/life11040308"], "source_candidate_identities": {}}

